"test": {"name": "tutorial2-playthrough", "kind": "rules", "opponent": "Human", "rounds": "10", "rules": "standard", "check": "scriptTutorial2", "question": "The second tutorial mission (Resources/Campaign/Scenarios/Tutorial 2.dat), played with the player's orders and recorded as a game is: the grunt boards the truck (told to load the supply unit), the supply unit boards (told to drive); the marked tile is outside the HQ's supply until the truck with supply aboard stands there; the grunt is put down in supply; the lookout (held, fed) is spotted; on turn 2 a recon car and a squad arrive, the squad boards the car; the lookout is destroyed, a grunt takes the village: the player wins. Then the campaign, on the mission assets as they are (Resources/Campaign/Missions): the result read from the game log earns its stars against Tutorial 2's pars; only Tutorial 1's flag is on the map at first, winning it unlocks Tutorial 2, stars once earned are kept, a mission blocked by an attempt is closed, and progress survives being saved and read back."}
}
